Build 035 (from the 034 run: std::bad_alloc on the GPU thread at 272 s, a 144 MiB request for the
RGBA8 scratch of one 6144x6144 ASTC slice kept as BC3, pool largest free block 9 MiB):
- ConvertImage decodes and compresses an ASTC slice in bands of rows once its RGBA8 scratch would
  pass 16 MiB; bands start on multiples of the ASTC block height and of 4, so the output is the same.
- EDEN_FLUSH_SITE (stdout every 5 s): the callers of Scheduler::Flush with the most flushes, for the
  70-90 submissions per frame seen in gameplay (031-034) with the GPU busy ~27%. Diagnostic only;
  EDEN_NX2_FLUSH_SITES_OFF disables it.

